    "graph": "perf-out/github-issue-discovery/automatic/psycopg-1502-first-check-20261126-b12/worker-analysis/graph.json",
    "findings": {
      "observation": "One reported silent-loopback connect/shutdown scenario with psycopg3.3.9, psycopg-pool3.3.3 and CPython3.12.16 accepts one connection. At0.604s after startup, asyncio.run is still in _cancel_all_tasks; worker0 is unfinished with cancelling()=1 at pool_async.py:679 awaiting q.get. Other pool workers are cancelled. Preparation and the sole run take76.80s. The diagnostic callback saves evidence and exits the process0.",
      "interpretation": "The actual Task address0x79ac9a18c100 independently matches asyncio.all_tasks, the pool-held worker reference and the generic CoroPerf creation/sample records. CoroPerf recovers start_connection_pool from the worker creation stack, absent from its later native/current wait stack and unavailable in native debug creation traces. The same worker has a scoped CancelledError observation in _connect/_add_connection before returning to queue wait. The focused capture has30 attributed observations; the catalogue highlights one cancellation observation and the last wait snapshot. The source report already describes cancellation swallowing; the added fact is historical application ownership.",
      "limits": "This proves a bounded shutdown stall, not infinite duration. asyncio.run does not return normally: the observer calls os._exit(0), closing owned loopback sockets. No pool.close workaround, fix, extra cancellation, reset path, other version or replay was tested. start_connection_pool is a submission helper introduced in this standalone harness. No exception-object identity was captured, so propagation records are not counted as distinct errors. A file-scoped exception probe supplements generic Task birth/sample capture; the original graph is preserved and the focused graph selects only the independently identified worker, without synthesizing runtime events."
    },
    "symptom_zh": "psycopg3.3.9、psycopg-pool3.3.3、CPython3.12.16 运行一次报告中的本机静默端口连接/退出场景，真实接受一个连接。启动后0.604秒，asyncio.run 仍在 _cancel_all_tasks 中，worker0 的 cancelling()=1，未结束且在 pool_async.py:679 等待 q.get；其他 worker 已取消。准备及唯一一次运行共76.80秒。诊断回调保存证据后直接退出进程0。",
    "reasoning_zh": "真实 Task 地址0x79ac9a18c100 在 asyncio.all_tasks、连接池持有的 worker 引用和通用 CoroPerf 创建/采样记录中一致。CoroPerf 从历史创建栈恢复 start_connection_pool，而稍后的原生/当前等待栈没有该入口，原生 debug 创建栈也未启用。同一 worker 先在 _connect/_add_connection 留下 CancelledError 观察，随后回到队列等待。聚焦捕获的30个观察均得到归属；目录展示一个取消观察与最后等待快照。报告已说明吞取消根因，新增事实是历史应用入口归属。",
    "limits_zh": "只证明有界退出卡顿，不声称永久等待。asyncio.run 没有正常返回；观察器调用 os._exit(0)，由进程退出关闭其本机套接字。未测试 pool.close 绕行、修复、额外取消、reset 路径、其他版本或重放。start_connection_pool 是该独立 harness 增加的提交辅助函数。没有异常对象身份，不能把传播记录算成多个独立错误。文件范围异常探针补充通用 Task 创建/采样；保留原始 graph，聚焦图只筛选原生引用独立确认的 worker，不生成运行时事件。"
  },
